WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:07.162
An aircraft returns to service because authorised people can show which
requirement, instruction and revision governs the work.

00:07.162 --> 00:14.353
The physical task may happen in a hangar, but the approval depends on a
controlled chain of documentary evidence.

00:14.353 --> 00:20.030
When that chain is fragmented across engineering instructions, maintenance
publications, service information and referenced standards,

00:20.030 --> 00:23.815
finding the right source becomes part of the engineering workload.

00:23.815 --> 00:29.870
Cortessa is designed to help reviewers investigate that evidence without
taking the decision away from them.

00:30.870 --> 00:33.963
A controlled change rarely lives in one document.

00:33.963 --> 00:41.310
A requirement can lead to an engineering order, an instruction, an illustrated
publication, a service communication and an external

00:41.310 --> 00:41.697
standard.

00:41.697 --> 00:45.563
Each may carry its own applicability, revision and approval state.

00:45.563 --> 00:49.043
The review problem is not simply finding matching words.

00:49.043 --> 00:56.777
It is establishing whether the source is current, whether the reference is
present, whether the terminology still aligns and whether

00:56.777 --> 01:01.030
the evidence applies to the aircraft, configuration and task under review.

01:02.030 --> 01:06.589
The credible starting point is one bounded engineering-change or
maintenance-instruction pack.

01:06.589 --> 01:14.049
Agree the authoritative documents, their revision history and the public,
synthetic or customer-cleared material that may be used.

01:14.049 --> 01:21.923
Define the questions, the expected source routes, the baseline review process
and the authorised engineers who will adjudicate results.

01:21.923 --> 01:24.824
Cortessa is evaluated against that fixed scope.

01:24.824 --> 01:31.870
It does not claim to understand every aircraft programme, replace an approved
data system or determine airworthiness.

01:32.870 --> 01:37.583
Cortessa runs on a dedicated sovereign workstation inside the agreed boundary.

01:37.583 --> 01:44.437
The approved corpus, ingestion pipeline, local index, on-device model and
source viewer remain on that machine.

01:44.437 --> 01:48.722
Runtime operation does not depend on a public cloud service.

01:48.722 --> 01:53.006
The organisation controls the permitted documents, users and security posture.

01:53.006 --> 01:56.005
Retrieval-only operation remains available as the floor.

01:56.005 --> 02:04.145
The purpose is bounded document investigation inside the existing engineering
environment, not a connection to aircraft systems or an

02:04.145 --> 02:05.430
expansion of access.

02:06.430 --> 02:09.799
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:09.799 --> 02:16.537
It works across the selected engineering pack rather than waiting for one
question at a time.

02:16.537 --> 02:22.433
It can surface supersession questions, orphaned references, terminology
differences, effectivity uncertainty and stale wording.

02:22.433 --> 02:28.750
Each candidate enters engineering review; it is not automatically an
airworthiness, regulatory or safety finding.

02:29.750 --> 02:34.176
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:34.176 --> 02:40.211
The engineer can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and check
revision, effectivity and applicability.

02:40.211 --> 02:45.039
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:45.039 --> 02:52.684
The engineer decides whether the issue is real, irrelevant, already controlled
or worth investigation, then records the outcome through

02:52.684 --> 02:53.891
the existing process.

02:53.891 --> 02:57.110
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish applicability.

02:58.110 --> 03:01.489
Configuration, effectivity and airworthiness significance require engineering
judgement.

03:01.489 --> 03:08.246
The responsible engineer decides which source governs, whether an apparent
conflict matters and what action follows.

03:08.246 --> 03:12.470
Cortessa makes the source route, uncertainty and review question visible.

03:12.470 --> 03:19.650
It does not approve technical data, release an aircraft, certify a repair or
sign an engineering decision.

03:19.650 --> 03:26.830
Existing design, quality and airworthiness authorities remain distinct, and
their formal records remain the record of approval.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.916
Reviewers need more than an answer.

03:29.916 --> 03:37.216
They need to see the source route, the document state and the policy governing
what the system is allowed to present.

03:37.216 --> 03:42.082
Identity, document currency, assertion policy and egress posture are part of
that operating picture.

03:42.082 --> 03:48.340
Local activity can be recorded in a ledger to support review of what the
system did and when.

03:48.340 --> 03:51.120
That record can contribute to an evidence package.

03:51.120 --> 03:57.030
It does not make a conclusion correct and does not replace the organisation's
configuration or approval record.

03:58.030 --> 04:01.273
Compare matched tasks against the current review baseline.

04:01.273 --> 04:09.381
Measure time to locate and open the governing source, reviewer effort, the
number and category of cited findings, reviewer agreement,

04:09.381 --> 04:13.030
appropriate refusals and the reproducibility of sampled source paths.

04:13.030 --> 04:16.679
Include difficult documents, superseded references and deliberately absent
evidence.

04:16.679 --> 04:19.111
Record corpus preparation and setup effort.

04:19.111 --> 04:27.625
The evaluation should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any consideration of a wider document

04:27.625 --> 04:28.030
estate.

04:29.030 --> 04:31.044
Bring one controlled engineering pack.

04:31.044 --> 04:34.668
Agree the reviewers, the baseline and the evidence standard.

04:34.668 --> 04:41.514
Test whether Cortessa makes the governing source easier to find and the
documentary questions easier to adjudicate.

04:41.514 --> 04:45.944
Cortessa claims no aircraft deployment, certification, dispatch improvement or
safety outcome.

04:45.944 --> 04:49.568
Those outcomes must never be assumed from a demonstration.

04:49.568 --> 04:52.790
Start a conversation about a scoped civil-aerospace evaluation.
